opentubex (0.37.4) stable; urgency=medium

  [ Highlights ]
  * The app takes on Material 3 Expressive, with rounder corners, tinted buttons
    and selections, springier motion, and bolder titles. Custom themes keep
    working.
  * A bell in the top bar keeps your live stream reminders, new uploads, and
    automatic downloads, which appear in the app instead of as system
    notifications while you use OpenTubeX. A new setting in General switches
    notifications to system only or off.

  [ More improvements ]
  * Exporting and importing large backups no longer freezes the app while the
    archive is created or read.
  * The cast menu lists the devices of every casting protocol together and,
    while casting, becomes a remote with seek and volume sliders, playback
    buttons, and subtitle choices.
  * You can now pin and unpin channels from their context menus.
  * Channels with TV shows now have a Shows tab. You can hide it in Distraction
    Free settings.
  * Right-clicking a collapsed tab group now opens a menu to expand it, close
    its tabs, or ungroup them.
  * Delete Old History on the History page can now delete your entire watch
    history with the new "All time" option.
  * The Material accent color picker now offers your system accent color, and
    the app follows it when you change it.
  * The About page and the update prompt now link to the new donation page,
    where you can support OpenTubeX through GitHub Sponsors or Liberapay.
  * Videos from other sites now work more like YouTube videos, with transcripts
    when they have captions and the same side panels and phone sheets.
  * Large watch histories and playlists are faster to edit, mark as watched, and
    sync.
  * OpenTubeX starts faster and stays responsive while loading a large watch
    history.
  * Layout settings in Appearance are now split into groups such as Interface,
    Tabs, Scrolling, and Notifications, and their switches, like those for video
    lists, sit in two columns.
  * OpenTubeX no longer contacts api.invidious.io at startup unless it uses a
    random Invidious instance.
  * Long YouTube playlists open and play without first downloading every page.
    Later pages load when playback, the playlist panel, or the progress bar
    reaches them.
  * Long video and playlist titles in lists and grids now stop after two lines
    with an ellipsis, so cards line up more evenly. Hover over a title to see
    all of it, or turn off Limit titles to two lines in Appearance settings.
  * 32-bit ARM (armv7l) Linux builds are no longer available, because Electron
    no longer supports them. 64-bit ARM (arm64) builds are still available.
  * The watch queue and transcripts of long videos open and scroll smoothly even
    with hundreds of queued videos or thousands of transcript lines.
  * Menus, tooltips, and dialogs now follow Material 3, with accent-colored
    icons and smooth open and close animations. Dialogs and bottom sheets also
    blur the page behind them.
  * A new layout setting hides in-app notifications that only confirm an action
    or report a status. Errors, warnings, reminders, and notifications with an
    action like Undo still appear, and background progress shows in the progress
    bar.
  * In the phone layout, the description now opens from a button like Comments,
    with a two-line excerpt and chips for its music, games, tags, and content
    labels.
  * More menus open as bottom sheets on phones, including the channel setting,
    cast, subscription settings, comment filter, comment sort, and "More
    options" menus.
  * Videos in the watch page playlist have a one-tap Remove from playlist button
    on their thumbnails again. Add to playlist moved into each video's menu.
  * The chapters panel next to the video now has a resize handle like the
    playlist panel, so you can drag it taller to see more chapters at once. It
    remembers the size you choose.
  * RSS feeds can now refresh automatically. New items are marked as new and
    show in the New feed, and items have a menu to open, download, or mark them
    as watched.
  * The RSS feed manager can now browse RSSHub, so picking an instance, a
    service and a username fills in the feed address. Feeds from sites that ask
    for a browser check now say so.
  * Checking for updates downloads far less data, about 0.4 MB instead of 5 MB
    when you're up to date.
  * A channel's subscription settings and the Subscription settings manager use
    chips you can toggle, keep the notification choices visible while the bell
    is off, and set the daily video limit with a stepper.
  * Watch progress of media opened by link, such as videos from other websites,
    now syncs between your devices along with your history.
  * The Ocean themes are now Tally Light and Tally Dark, matching the website's
    new look. Their accent color defaults to red and can be changed to a preset,
    a custom color, or your system's accent color where available.
  * Twitch live chat uses less CPU in busy channels.
  * With the Local API, Up Next now shows when a video is a collaboration
    between several channels. Middle-clicking a collaboration's channel names
    now lists the collaborators instead of doing nothing.
  * You can now set the height of vertical tabs in Appearance settings.
  * The new Video descriptions setting in Distraction Free settings and Quick
    Settings hides descriptions, keeps them collapsed, or opens them expanded.

  [ Fixed bugs ]
  * The App font list opens right away instead of freezing for several seconds
    when many fonts are installed.
  * When playback drops frames, automatic quality now steps down to a lower
    resolution of the same codec instead of switching to a codec that is harder
    to decode, such as AV1.
  * Captions grow and shrink with the player, so they cover the same share of
    the video in a window, in fullscreen, and in the mini player.
  * Older completed, queued, and paused downloads no longer disappear from
    Downloads after a restart, and a download whose files can't all be removed
    stays listed with an error message.
  * Downloaded videos now start playing within a few seconds when YouTube can't
    be reached, even while the rest of the internet works. Their details fill in
    once YouTube responds again.
  * A missing or wrong external player now shows a message that it couldn't be
    started instead of crashing OpenTubeX with an error dialog.
  * Failed or incomplete comment loads now offer a retry instead of reporting no
    comments or repeatedly retrying. The phone comments panel no longer
    duplicates its refresh and sort controls.
  * Invidious instances with special characters such as @, spaces, or % in the
    username or password of their URL now sign in correctly.
  * Buttons, selected controls, and accent-colored highlights are now easier to
    read with light main and secondary colors, such as Light Blue, Pink, and
    Green.
  * The app no longer crashes when you press a menu shortcut, such as Ctrl+, to
    open the settings, after watching a video.
  * When Start Videos Automatically is off, the next playlist or recommended
    video now starts after the countdown or Play Now, while videos you open
    yourself stay paused. Looping a playlist with one video now replays it every
    time.
  * Videos with captions in your preferred caption language now show those
    captions instead of the auto-translation you last picked in the player.
  * Videos and Shorts no longer take minutes to open while YouTube rate-limits
    your connection, and other requests no longer stall behind one that cannot
    succeed.
  * Setting Reduced Motion to Force off now brings back every animation when
    your system asks for reduced motion, and Force on stops the remaining tab,
    sheet and gesture animations.
  * RSS feeds that loaded before no longer reload after a restart when Fetch
    Feed on Startup is off, and show their saved items instead.
  * A failed search history import no longer erases your existing search
    history.
  * Videos keep loading at their selected quality on slow or high-latency
    connections, instead of dropping to 360p and reloading over and over.
  * Background subscription refresh no longer reports errors for channels
    without Shorts, live streams, or posts, or mistakes their regular uploads
    for Shorts or live streams.

 -- OpenTubeX contributors <info@opentubex.org>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:37:02 +0000
